 INNER CLASS

Interview Questions

1. What is inner class?
-->An inner class is a class declared inside another class or interface. It helps group related classes together and can directly
   access the members (including private members) of the outer class.

    Syntax:
    
    class Outer {
        class Inner {
            void display() {
                System.out.println("Inside Inner Class");
            }
        }
    }






2. Can we declare an inner class inside an interface?
-->Yes.

          An interface can contain an inner class. Such a class is public and static by default.
          
          Example:
          
          interface Test {
              class Demo {
                  void show() {
                      System.out.println("Inner class inside interface");
                  }
              }
          }
          
          public class Main {
              public static void main(String[] args) {
                  Test.Demo obj = new Test.Demo();
                  obj.show();
              }
          }
          
          Output:
          
          Inner class inside interface



3. Can an interface be declared inside a class?
-->Yes.
      
      A class can contain an interface.
      
      Example:
      
      class Outer {
      
          interface MyInterface {
              void display();
          }
      }
      
      class Demo implements Outer.MyInterface {
          public void display() {
              System.out.println("Interface inside class");
          }
      
          public static void main(String[] args) {
              Demo obj = new Demo();
              obj.display();
          }
      }
      
      Output:
      
      Interface inside class





4. How can you access the outer class object inside an inner class?
-->Use:
     
     OuterClass.this
     
     Example:
     
     class Outer {
         int x = 100;
     
         class Inner {
             void show() {
                 System.out.println(Outer.this.x);
             }
         }
     
         public static void main(String[] args) {
             Outer o = new Outer();
             Outer.Inner i = o.new Inner();
             i.show();
         }
     }
     
     Output:
     
     100




5. What is the fully qualified name of an inner class?
-->The fully qualified name is:

      OuterClass.InnerClass
      
      Example:
      
      class Outer {
          class Inner {
          }
      }
      
      Object creation:
      
      Outer.Inner obj;



6. Can an inner class be abstract, final, or static?
-->Yes.
        
        abstract → Yes
        final → Yes
        static → Yes (only if it is a static nested class, not a regular member inner class)
        
        Example:
        
        class Outer {
        
            abstract class A {
                abstract void show();
            }
        
            final class B {
            }
        
            static class C {
            }
        }



7. Can an inner class override methods of its outer class?
-->Yes.

       If the inner class extends the outer class, it can override inherited methods.
       
       Example:
       
       class Outer {
       
           void show() {
               System.out.println("Outer");
           }
       
           class Inner extends Outer {
               @Override
               void show() {
                   System.out.println("Inner");
               }
           }
       
           public static void main(String[] args) {
               Outer o = new Outer();
               Outer.Inner i = o.new Inner();
               i.show();
           }
       }
       
       Output:
       
       Inner






8. How do you access a private inner class from another class?
-->You cannot directly access a private inner class from another class.
      It can only be accessed through public methods of the outer class.
      
      Example:
      
      class Outer {
      
          private class Inner {
              void show() {
                  System.out.println("Private Inner");
              }
          }
      
          void display() {
              Inner obj = new Inner();
              obj.show();
          }
      }
      
      public class Main {
          public static void main(String[] args) {
              Outer obj = new Outer();
              obj.display();
          }
      }
      
      Output:
      
      Private Inner





9. Can an inner class shadow a variable name from its outer class?
-->Yes.
       An inner class can declare a variable with the same name as the outer class variable.
       
       Use:
           x → Inner class variable
           Outer.this.x → Outer class variable

Example:      
      class Outer {
      
          int x = 10;
      
          class Inner {
              int x = 20;
      
              void display() {
                  System.out.println(x);
                  System.out.println(Outer.this.x);
              }
          }
      
          public static void main(String[] args) {
              Outer o = new Outer();
              Outer.Inner i = o.new Inner();
              i.display();
          }
      }

Output:
   20
   10






10. How can we resolve naming conflicts between outer and inner class members?
-->Use:
      this.member → Inner class member
      OuterClass.this.member → Outer class member

Example:
       class Outer {
       
           int value = 100;
       
           class Inner {
               int value = 200;
       
               void show() {
                   System.out.println(this.value);
                   System.out.println(Outer.this.value);
               }
           }
       
           public static void main(String[] args) {
               Outer o = new Outer();
               Outer.Inner i = o.new Inner();
               i.show();
           }
       }

Output:
    200
    100
